# Tenant Management System - Cursor Rules

## Project Overview
A web-based tenant management system for a rental property business.
Built with Laravel 13, Blade, Tailwind CSS, Alpine.js, and Flowbite.

## Tech Stack
- Backend: Laravel 13, PHP 8.3
- Frontend: Blade templates, Tailwind CSS, Alpine.js, Flowbite
- Database: MySQL
- Auth: Laravel Breeze (Blade)
- Local Server: Laragon (Windows)

## User Roles
- admin — property owner, full access
- tenant — limited access to own lease, payments, notifications

## Database Tables
users: id, name, email, password, role (enum: admin/tenant), remember_token, timestamps
password_reset_tokens: email, token, created_at
properties: id, name, address, description, timestamps, deleted_at
units: id, property_id (FK), unit_number, unit_type, rent_price, status (enum: vacant/occupied), timestamps, deleted_at
tenants: id, user_id (FK), phone_number, emergency_contact_name, emergency_contact_number, address, timestamps, deleted_at
leases: id, tenant_id (FK), unit_id (FK), start_date, end_date, monthly_rent, deposit_amount, deposit_status (enum: held/returned/forfeited), status (enum: active/completed/terminated), timestamps, deleted_at
payments: id, lease_id (FK), amount_paid, due_date, payment_date (nullable), payment_method (enum: cash/gcash/bank_transfer/maya), proof_of_payment (nullable, file path), verified_at (nullable timestamp), status (enum: pending/paid/late/rejected), remarks (nullable), timestamps
notifications: id, user_id (FK), type, data (JSON), read_at (nullable), timestamps

## Relationships
- User hasOne Tenant
- User hasMany Notifications
- Property hasMany Units
- Unit belongsTo Property
- Unit hasMany Leases
- Tenant belongsTo User
- Tenant hasMany Leases
- Lease belongsTo Tenant
- Lease belongsTo Unit
- Lease hasMany Payments
- Payment belongsTo Lease

## Coding Conventions
- Use Laravel MVC architecture
- Controllers go in App\Http\Controllers
- Admin controllers go in App\Http\Controllers\Admin
- Tenant controllers go in App\Http\Controllers\Tenant
- Use Route::middleware(['auth', 'role:admin']) for admin routes
- Use Route::middleware(['auth', 'role:tenant']) for tenant routes
- Blade views go in resources/views
- Admin views go in resources/views/admin
- Tenant views go in resources/views/tenant
- Shared layouts go in resources/views/layouts
- Use SoftDeletes on Property, Unit, Tenant, Lease models
- Always use $fillable in models
- Use Tailwind CSS utility classes only, no custom CSS unless necessary
- Use Flowbite components for UI (modals, tables, badges, dropdowns)
- Use Alpine.js for interactivity (no jQuery)
- File uploads stored in storage/app/public/payments

## Status Badge Colors (Tailwind + Flowbite)
- paid / active / occupied = green
- pending / vacant = yellow
- late / rejected / terminated = red
- completed = blue
- held = gray

## DO NOT
- Do not use jQuery
- Do not use Vue or React
- Do not use any payment gateway
- Do not create overly complex logic
- Do not use inline styles
- Do not skip $fillable in models